From: OpenIRD contributors
Subject: [PATCH] timeconst: do not call defined() on an array

kernel/timeconst.pl tests "defined(@val)" to see whether the canned table
had an entry for this HZ.  Perl deprecated defined(@array) in 5.6 and made
it a fatal error in 5.22, so on any current build host the script dies and
kernel/timeconst.h is never generated:

  Can't use 'defined(@array)' (Maybe you should just omit the defined()?)

An array in boolean context is true when it has elements, which is what
the test meant.  Mainline later made the same change.

Origin: gpl-derived
---
--- a/kernel/timeconst.pl
+++ b/kernel/timeconst.pl
@@ -370,7 +370,7 @@
 	}
 
 	@val = @{$canned_values{$hz}};
-	if (!defined(@val)) {
+	if (!@val) {
 		@val = compute_values($hz);
 	}
 	output($hz, @val);
